        "analysis": "Across all three development pairs, structural checks pass while visible errors remain. The chaise has disconnected upholstery/frame contours and an offscreen foreground chair; the bunk room has misplaced ceiling/lamp features and weak light-dark separation; the classroom has close board bounds but loses the broad contrasting wipe patterns and rich surface colors. These are not explained by one camera correction. Before prescribing appearance changes, inspect actual shader assignments: the classroom program selects panels by dimensions and chooses their material using local obj.location.x after parenting. A mistaken assignment is a competing explanation to insufficient procedural contrast or excessive illumination. This audit can distinguish assignment facts from appearance hypotheses, without claiming shader defaults measure rendered brightness.",
